course: dictionary
lesson: 7038
title: Partnership: working together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A partnership is when two or more people or groups work together as partners. In «The school works in partnership with the zoo», the clue is the phrase «in partnership with», which shows the school and the zoo doing a job side by side.
explain: Partnership can also mean a business owned and run by two or more partners, or a pair who work or play well together. In cricket, a batting partnership counts the runs two batters score together.
explain: Use the swap check. In «Many fungi in the soil join tree roots with fine threads; this partnership is called mycorrhiza», put in «working together» and the sentence still makes sense, so partnership means working together.
fact: Partnership is a noun: one partnership, and more than one partnership.
fact: «In partnership with» means working together with someone.
fact: «Form a partnership» means to start working together as partners.
fact: «A good partnership» means a pair who work or play well together.
fact: In a business partnership, the partners own and run the business together and may share the profits.
exercise: «The school works in partnership with the zoo.» What does partnership mean here? | A fight between two groups | A large building | A rule about how long to play | *Working together with someone as partners
exercise: In cricket, what does a batting partnership count? | The wickets taken by the bowler | The number of balls bowled | *The runs scored by two batters together | The score of one batter alone
exercise: «Influencers are often paid to praise products; look for «paid partnership».» What does «paid partnership» suggest? | A free gift for everyone | *The influencer was paid to praise the product | The fungus is hungry | A school trip paid for by parents
test: «Many fungi in the soil join tree roots with fine threads; this partnership is called mycorrhiza.» What does partnership mean here? | Separating to be alone | *Both sides working together, each helping the other | Fast and hard running | A kind of mushroom only
test: Two friends open a shop together and share the profits. What is this called? | A fungus | *A business partnership | A batting partnership | A paid advertisement
exam: Why should you look for the words «paid partnership» on a post? | *To know the influencer was paid to praise the product | To see where the fungus grows | To learn a new cricket score | To find the cheapest price
